@@ -17,73 +9 @@ SkyFire provides a separate World of Warcraft Mists of Pandaria 5.4.8 realm, bas
-## Architecture
-
-```mermaid
-flowchart TD
-    Client[Compatible 5.4.8 client] -->|TCP 3724| Auth[SkyFire authserver]
-    Client -->|TCP 8085| World[SkyFire worldserver]
-    Auth -->|Authentication data| SQL[(MySQL 8.4)]
-    World -->|World and character data| SQL
-    World -->|dbc, db2, maps, vmaps, mmaps| Data[(Longhorn RWX)]
-    Extract[Reviewed client-data extraction] -->|Generated assets| Data
-```
-
-The realm has one authserver and one worldserver. They use selected host ports on a reviewed node instead of exposing all traffic through an HTTP ingress. The worldserver also requires its complete extracted asset directories before normal startup.
-
-## Source and build provenance
-
-The image workflow builds the SkyFire core from the source revision recorded in [`ops/mop-images/skyfire.ref`](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/blob/main/ops/mop-images/skyfire.ref). Its database inputs are verified against the reviewed upstream release. Image build and smoke tests precede a separate image-reference pull request; applying a published image to the live realm remains a reviewed GitOps action.
-
-For the canonical setup expectations, see [`apps/mop/README.md`](https://github.com/RovxBot/homelab-infra/blob/main/apps/mop/README.md).
-
-## Database and client assets
-
-MySQL persists authentication, character and world information on a dedicated volume. Database bootstrap applies the required base schema and approved upstream updates for a fresh dataset. Runtime credentials are injected from a SOPS-encrypted Secret.
-
-The shared data volume contains `dbc`, `db2`, `maps`, `vmaps` and `mmaps` derived from a compatible client source. Missing or mismatched data can prevent server startup or break world movement even when the container image is healthy.
-
-Two extraction CronJob definitions are present:
-
-- `skyfire-client-extract` prepares complete datasets, including resource-intensive map generation.
-- `skyfire-client-db2-extract` repairs the narrower DB2 extraction case without regenerating all map data.
-
-**Both CronJobs are suspended** by default and are intended for separately reviewed, one-off Jobs. Their cron expressions are placeholders for Kubernetes CronJob resources, not evidence that scheduled extraction is active.
-
-> [!CAUTION]
-> Full extraction writes the shared data directories and can replace previously generated assets. Do not unsuspend the job or start an extraction against production storage without confirming the client build, source volume, a verified backup and a maintenance window.
-
-## Network and identity
-
-The native client protocol is not proxied through Cloudflare Tunnel. Client access depends on the intended LAN/edge routing and native game authentication; no HTTP identity provider protects the game TCP listener. Database credentials must remain separate from client connection settings.
-
-Keep the WotLK and MoP host-port/node placement decisions coordinated, as their applications use the same conventional game port numbers on **different** selected nodes. Changing either node selector or port mapping requires a routing review. See [[Network Architecture]] and [[AzerothCore WotLK]].
-
-## Recovery and maintenance
-
-The database and extracted client-data PVCs require distinct recovery plans. Longhorn can restore the underlying volumes, but a recovered realm must also pass SQL startup, database compatibility, client login, map loading and world-entry tests.
-
-Do not perform unreviewed schema downgrades after a newer SkyFire image has applied migrations. Prefer a test restore into separate volumes before committing to production replacement.
-
-## Operate
-
-```bash
-kubectl -n mop get deployments,statefulsets,pods,services,pvc
-kubectl -n mop get cronjobs
-kubectl -n flux-system get kustomization apps-mop
-kubectl -n mop get pods -o wide
-```
-
-The extractor CronJobs should remain suspended outside an approved one-time operation. A Ready Pod alone does not establish that a compatible 5.4.8 client can authenticate and enter the world.
-
-| Symptom | First investigation |
-| --- | --- |
-| Authserver cannot start | Database readiness, credentials and schema version |
-| Client can authenticate but cannot enter world | Worldserver readiness, host port and advertised realm address |
-| Worldserver reports missing maps | Shared data PVC and extracted directory completeness |
-| DB2-derived gameplay data absent | Existing extraction provenance and reviewed narrow repair procedure |
-| Extractor exceeds node capacity | Requested CPU/memory, scratch space and client source |
-| Image upgrade fails | Source revision, database migration and image smoke-test evidence |
